		(uuid "65976b31-85d9-3806-f879-68813a2843d0")
	)
	(text_box "Core regulator (1.1 V): Raspberry Pi's parts\nand layout, copied exactly\n(gen/rpi_minimal). L1 is polarity-marked:\nits dot must sit as their footprint shows."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 156.21 35.56 0)
		(size 39.37 10.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "75172a13-fb45-3b6e-a428-e5733acb987e")
	)
	(text_box "Open-drain: a line is\nasserted by driving\nits pin low and\nreleased by letting\ngo. NRFD, NDAC and SRQ\nare wired-OR on every\nbus, and the Lite\ntreats the other lines\nthe same way, so it\nnever needs to know\nwho else is driving."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 344.17 173.99 0)
		(size 24.13 21.59)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "92a34068-6ce4-87b7-df78-07ed1da378ba")
	)
	(text_box "BOOT: hold it while plugging in to start\nthe RP2354A's USB bootloader. Rarely\nneeded: 'picotool reboot -f -u' gets\nthere from software. RUN stays open: it\nhas its own pull-up inside the RP2354A\n(datasheet table 1677), and the Debug\nProbe resets the chip over SWD."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.26 163.83 0)
		(size 36.83 15.24)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9856c332-3543-52c5-727b-3172b5e921a0")
	)
	(text_box "USB-C. Takes 5 V, about 40 mA:\nthe RP2354A and its LEDs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 114.3 0)
		(size 30.48 6.35)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
