				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e8718429-4c09-96fc-1b47-fe1549f98e49")
	)
	(text_box "An RP2354A runs the IEEE-488 handshake and talks to the host\nover USB as a Prologix-compatible serial controller. GPiBridge\nLite has no bus transceivers: each of the sixteen bus lines\nmeets an RP2354A pin through 100 R. The firmware drives them\nopen-drain (low to assert, let go to release), and the pads'\noutput is forced low in hardware, so no pin can drive a line\nhigh. That carries one instrument, or a few on a short cable: 12\nmA sinks against the standard's 48 mA, and no terminations of\nits own. For a full bus, GPiBridge. The plug hangs under the\nboard; everything else is on top."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 238.76 0)
		(size 71.12 24.13)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "f49478dd-98d9-61ad-a035-049e5212e470")
	)
	(text_box "USB (yellow) and ERR (red) are the\nfirmware's. Both are low-voltage\ncolours, so a 3.3 V pin lights them\nthrough 330 R (3 mA)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.26 205.74 0)
		(size 33.02 10.16)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
